 "note": "Ruling R11 (decision A9): the known criteria of a cleanup policy are lastBlobUpdatedDays and lastDownloadedDays, each a whole number of 1 or more, or absent or null. A request (create, save, preview; op request) with a criterion of another name, or with a value that is no such number, is refused with 400 at criteria.<name>, one with no criterion set with 400 at criteria. A stored policy (op stored) that holds a criterion of another name is no error: it is listed, never runs (counted as refused), and its unknown criteria are named. The names retainDays and keepLatest are invented for the unknown criterion; no source names one. Two answers are choices of this package that no source fixes: a whole number is at most 2^53, the largest one a float64 holds exactly, so 1e300 is refused; and the refusal at criteria comes only when no other criteria refusal does, as in the mock of the interface, so retainDays alone is refused at criteria.retainDays only. The test decodes each criteria object twice, with numbers as float64 and as json.Number, and decodes the stored criteria of a save (op save) with the other decoder, so that 30 and 30.0 are equal across the two. Ruling R11b (R6 holds for the criteria, op save under the rows R11 and R6): a save never refuses a value the stored policy already holds. A criterion of any name whose value equals the stored value of that name is not refused, an unknown name among them; the policy keeps it and never runs. A new unknown name, and a changed value of a stored unknown name, are refused as before. The refusal at criteria does not come when the sent criteria equal the stored ones key by key; a key with null on one side only makes them differ, a choice of this package. A create and a preview have no stored criteria (op request), where R11 holds as built.",
